In State::new, before SetInputType, replace lines 355-357 with:
```rust
let attributes = transform.GetAttributes().context("decoder attributes")?;
// CODECAPI_AVLowLatencyMode has the same GUID as MF_LOW_LATENCY
attributes
    .SetUINT32(&CODECAPI_AVLowLatencyMode, 1)
    .context("enable decoder low-latency mode")?;
```
This is how Chromium and Firefox configure this MFT. Do not ignore the result. With low latency on, the MFT emits one picture per access unit and the test gets 16 pictures, well over the 8 it needs. Optionally assert in the test that the first IDR decodes to a picture immediately, so latency regressions are caught.
